    "body": "## Problem\n\nA `developer` (or `system`) message with empty string content or a missing `content` key passes Pydantic validation (empty string is a valid `str`) but crashes downstream renderers with a **500 Internal Server Error** — and the error body can leak internal state (e.g. `_image_indices`):\n\n```json\n{\"error\":{\"message\":\"Invalid message for role `developer`: {'content': '', 'role': 'developer', '_image_indices': []}\",\"type\":\"InternalServerError\"}}\n```\n\nMeanwhile, `content: null` is correctly rejected with a **400** by Pydantic's string type validation. The gap: empty string and missing key slip past validation and explode at the rendering layer.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a `model_validator(mode=\"before\")` on `ChatCompletionRequest` that rejects developer/system messages with empty or whitespace-only `content`, raising a `ValueError` (→ 400) at the protocol layer — consistent with how `content: null` is already handled.\n\nThis is a ~15-line addition, placed alongside the existing message pre-processing validators.\n\nFixes #65357\n\n## Testing\n\nReproduced on nightly `v0.33.0rc1.dev573`:\n\n| Input | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `{\"role\":\"developer\",\"content\":\"\"}` | 500 + leaked `_image_indices` | 400 |\n| `{\"role\":\"developer\"}` (no content key) | 500 | 400 |\n| `{\"role\":\"developer\",\"content\":null}` | 400 (already worked) | 400 |\n| `{\"role\":\"developer\",\"content\":\"valid\"}` | 200 | 200 (no change) |\n",
